{
 "about": "The node<->MC envelope rule (contracts.md §5): every frame here is decoded by mcp/brx_mcp/mc/envelope.py decode() and app/src/transport/envelope.js decode(), and both must give `expect`: \"ok\" or the EnvelopeError reason. `frame` is serialised as compact JSON; `text` is sent as written. Then each `fill` replaces its `token` with `with` repeated `times` times. `differs` names a language that cannot agree, with the reason in `why`. Hand-kept: add a case when either validator changes.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "a death fact as the phone's Transport.send writes it",
   "direction": "node",
   "frame": {
    "v": 1,
    "kind": "event",
    "id": "e1",
    "t": 1700000000000,
    "body": {
     "type": "death",
     "match_id": "m1",
     "shooter_num": 19,
     "shooter_team": 2,
     "t": 1700000000000,
     "node_id": "n1",
     "player_id": "p1"
    },
    "seq": 1
   },
   "expect": "ok",
   "why": "envelope-cases.test.mjs rebuilds this frame through the real Transport.send, so a check that refuses a real phone frame fails here"
  },
  {
